{"source_id":"W4392938786","title":"The Effect of Laptop Note-Taking on Students’ Learning Performance, Strategies, and Satisfaction","year":2024,"abstract":"The pervasiveness of laptops in the classroom has sparked debate about their effectiveness for note-taking. This study investigated the effects of laptop versus longhand note-taking on learning performance, note-taking strategies, and satisfaction among 120 university students. Participants took notes during a video lecture in either longhand or on a laptop, and half in each condition were given the opportunity to review their notes before a comprehension test. Results revealed no significant main effect of note-taking medium on test performance, and no significant medium by review interaction. Students in the laptop condition recorded more verbatim content, but this did not translate into performance differences. Satisfaction was higher in the laptop condition."}
